---
/**
 * TeamCards. The founding-team bio cards (full-height blended photo panel +
 * bio), shared between the public /team page and the investor-pitch team page
 * so both render the exact same cards from one source.
 */
import BioPhoto from "./BioPhoto.astro";
---

<div class="reveal glass-bright rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-stretch">
    <BioPhoto src="/headshots/rio.jpg" alt="Rio Bold" />
    <div class="flex-1 p-8 md:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl text-text-primary font-medium">Rio Bold</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted font-tech mt-1">Cofounder & Architect</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-3">
        <a href="mailto:info@oscen.ai" class="text-[11px] font-tech text-accent-blue/70 hover:text-accent-blue transition-colors">info@oscen.ai</a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/rio-bold" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[11px] font-tech text-accent-blue/70 hover:text-accent-blue transition-colors">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Marine Corps veteran. <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">13 years of professional software engineering</span> across multiple Fortune 500 companies,
          building AI integrations, enterprise business processes, and full-stack systems at scale.
          Combined with nearly a decade of independent research in computational neuroscience, distributed systems, and real-time sensor fusion.
        </p>
        <p>
          5 years of planning and architectural design, then 7 months of focused build to bring the complete OSCEN architecture from concept to 1M-neuron deployment.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Domain expertise:</span> Spiking neural network theory, STDP/BCM learning rules,
          sparse matrix computation (CSR/COO), real-time event-driven systems, neuromorphic hardware constraints (Loihi, SpiNNaker),
          robotic motor control, and sensor fusion pipelines.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every architectural decision. Every learning mechanism. Every line of code.
          Sensory gateway, brain simulation, motor output, cognitive action channel, speech motor, developmental phases,
          persistence layer, monitoring pipeline, and 660+ tests.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="reveal glass-bright rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-stretch">
    <BioPhoto src="/headshots/adam.jpg" alt="Adam Hamersky" />
    <div class="flex-1 p-8 md:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl text-text-primary font-medium">Adam Hamersky</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted font-tech mt-1">Cofounder & Operations</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-3">
        <a href="mailto:info@oscen.ai" class="text-[11px] font-tech text-accent-blue/70 hover:text-accent-blue transition-colors">info@oscen.ai</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Marine Corps veteran</span> with a record of leading people and running fleets under pressure.
          Served as Chief Motor Pool Dispatcher for the 7th Marine Regiment, coordinating personnel, vehicles, and mission readiness against tight operational windows.
        </p>
        <p>
          Brings that same discipline and mission focus to building the brain that will move the next generation of robots, turning architectural ambition into a fundable, hireable, deployable company.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Operating focus:</span> fleet logistics, program management, partnership development,
          and the operational footing required to take OSCEN from research artifact to commercial deployment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every operational decision. Every hire. Every milestone.
          The mission discipline that keeps the build on track.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="reveal glass-bright rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-stretch">
    <BioPhoto src="/headshots/rob.jpg" alt="Robert Robancho" />
    <div class="flex-1 p-8 md:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl text-text-primary font-medium">Robert Robancho</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted font-tech mt-1">Partner, Intelligence & Threat</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-3">
        <a href="mailto:info@oscen.ai" class="text-[11px] font-tech text-accent-blue/70 hover:text-accent-blue transition-colors">info@oscen.ai</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Marine Corps veteran</span> with a record of evaluating and neutralizing asymmetric threats in high-stakes environments.
          Built foundational expertise in tactical military intelligence, reading adversary intent under time pressure and translating ambiguous signals into defensive posture.
        </p>
        <p>
          Transitioned to the consulting sector as an analyst at Deloitte, where he led complex operational logistics and data tracking for United States Space Force contracts.
          Recognized with the 2026 Charlie Allen Achievement Edwin Land Industry Award for outsized impact on the national security mission.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Operating focus:</span> intelligence frameworks, threat modeling, OPSEC discipline, security clearance management,
          and hardening emerging physical AI platforms against modern vulnerabilities. Bridges ground-level tactical realities with high-level strategic intelligence.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every intelligence assessment. Every threat surface. Every hardened deployment.
          The OPSEC discipline that keeps the architecture defensible from day one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="reveal glass-bright rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-stretch">
    <BioPhoto src="/headshots/sully.jpg" alt="Sully Regmi" />
    <div class="flex-1 p-8 md:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl text-text-primary font-medium">Sully Regmi</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted font-tech mt-1">Research Scientist</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-3">
        <a href="mailto:info@oscen.ai" class="text-[11px] font-tech text-accent-blue/70 hover:text-accent-blue transition-colors">info@oscen.ai</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Neuroscience and emotion-science researcher.</span> Holds a degree in neuroscience.
          Studies how emotion and social judgment arise from neurocognitive processes at UC Santa Barbara's Yu Emotion Science Lab,
          with earlier work on visual attention and eye-tracking at UCSB's Vision and Image Understanding Lab.
          Brings that grounding in how the brain processes signals together with a machine-learning practice across natural language processing and computer vision.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the OSCEN team, contributes on the speech and language side, connecting how biological auditory and speech-motor pathways learn
          to the platform's spiking implementation, and supporting the research program and experimental validation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Research focus:</span> natural language processing, computer vision,
          emotion and affective modeling, and reproducible evaluation of the learning system.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
